  "set": "payload-signatures",
  "what_this_proves": "That an implementation signs the same bytes for the same payload. Pins key ordering, string escaping, number formatting, null handling and signature encoding together. Ed25519 is deterministic, so any correct implementation reproduces these exact signatures.",
  "rules": [
    "Signing bytes are RFC 8785 (JCS): UTF-8, object keys sorted, no insignificant whitespace, numbers in shortest round-trippable form, array order preserved.",
    "The artifact's own signature field is never part of the bytes being signed.",
    "A null-valued field is signed as null, not omitted (see groupId in the ticket).",
    "Signatures are base64url with no padding. Standard base64 is NOT accepted.",
    "The AS signs the mandate and the ticket. The Mandate Owner signs the projection and the approval. Each vector names which key signed it, and the mandate's \"issuer\" field is the AS key's own DID — so a verifier resolves the key from the artifact. Conditional projection fields (above_cap_caps, above_cap_approvers, disclose_fields, intent_disclosure_hash) are present exactly when the mandate carries them."
  ],
